  "id": "Compound::DB01062 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Oxybutynin exhibits a strong binding interaction with Cyp2c8 and Cyp3a5, which are both involved in the metabolism of arachidonic acid. This binding leads to the activation of arachidonic acid monooxygenase and epoxygenase activities, which are ultimately linked to the participation of Cyp2d6. These pathways suggest that Oxybutynin may influence Cyp2d6 through a shared metabolic substrate, arachidonic acid, and its downstream enzymatic activities. The evidence from the three paths is consistent, with similar scores, indicating a robust mechanistic link between Oxybutynin and Cyp2d6. The overlapping roles of Cyp2c8 and Cyp3a5 in arachidonic acid metabolism support the hypothesis that Oxybutynin exerts its effects on Cyp2d6 via a common metabolic pathway. The integration of these findings suggests that Oxybutynin may modulate Cyp2d6 activity through the enzymatic conversion of arachidonic acid, potentially affecting lipid metabolism and other downstream processes.",
